+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool input validation protects executors and gives the model actionable feedback when it sends malformed arguments.
+
+- The registry rejects missing required fields, wrong types and invalid enum values with a ToolResponse identifying the property and constraint without exposing values; valid input, including extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged and without defaults or coercion. ([validated by: rejects invalid input and passes valid input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14))
+- Registering a static tool with an uncompilable schema throws an error naming the tool. ([validated by: rejects an invalid static schema when the tool is registered](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L42))
+- A function-valued definition is validated against the schema resolved for each call. ([validated by: validates each call against the current dynamic definition](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49))
